#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:5
#: c3b1d16a75ec48838082b6dd17c50512
msgid "Fly-By-Wire Low Altitude Limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:7
#: 0ebbe3450f35469389999fc511875f94
msgid "This function of Plane allows you to set a minimum altitude for FBWB and CRUISE modes (even if you don't have airspeed sensor) which your airplane will try to stay above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:11
#: 69ea1cd3f1be4ecc8ed201357f4e4d51
msgid "When :ref:`CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR<CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR>` is enabled, if your airplane goes lower than defined altitude relative to HOME, it will level up and/or climb back to this altitude. After it is reached you will regain altitude control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:15
#: d9c1bbe01f50414d972dc9756cb53d0e
msgid "the minimum MSL altitude target will be the higher of: this altitude, or the current altitude target above terrain in FBWB or CRUISE modes if :ref:`common-terrain-following` is enabled, or the :ref:`FENCE_ALT_MIN<FENCE_ALT_MIN>` above HOME if that fence (See :ref:`common-geofencing-landing-page`) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:18
#: 1a7964d5c5ee447aa88948edd7d2a354
msgid "Use for R/C training"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:20
#: 6e2959b9247d4fc68408a31500e76681
msgid "This function will help those of us who doesn't have that much flying skills to fly safely. It is really useful for FPV flying as FBWB or CRUISE modes provide easy control and the :ref:`CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR<CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR>` limit will help you avoid crashing into the ground ;-)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:25
#: e115b35a3c294223bd934d4d11a24c92
msgid "`Here <http://youtu.be/9wysVRrOmcQ>`__ is a video demo. APM is in FBW-B mode and I hold pitch all the way DOWN! until the very end of video. Minimum alt was set 30 meters above home altitude, so you can see ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:31
#: 4830fa75b48346ebbf4fe895e31d9963
msgid "How to setup Alt Limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:33
#: 96074531b27d468d860c4ed656627711
msgid "Using your APM Mission Planner you will have to set parameter :ref:`CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR<CRUISE_ALT_FLOOR>` to the desired alt **in meters!** If it is **0** then it is turned off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:38
#: 4c14c664dba347aeb2e10ff5d7bcf720
msgid "Choosing the right altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:40
#: 6ab44f4fe6204ad6856129584dfd7fdd
msgid "Desired altitude should be set very carefully. As we know our planes can't react immediately, so we have to choose altitude with this in mind. Using 3000 (30 meters) is recommended for flights over pretty flat terrain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:45
#: b0d5bf66c8e14312a5d408ab0f5274e3
msgid "Landing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/fly-by-wire-low-altitude-limit.rst:47
#: 4d8f3582d93f49ce8b169fd5296e99cb
msgid "In order to land your plane you will need to disable this feature by changing your flightmode to anything other than FBWB or CRUISE. FBWA, STABILIZE, or MANUAL modes are always the preferred modes for a manual landing, in any case."
msgstr ""
